"""Detect UTF-8 fragments, plus document-initial control/line-ending tokens.

Positive values mark unfinished UTF-8 characters, especially the penultimate
byte of a three-byte character. A continuation-only token is stronger than a
fused initial fragment. Unicode regions and leading spaces set the scale.
Completed text has a near-zero baseline. Only the unfinished suffix crosses
token boundaries. These fragments need not be corrupt text: the tokenizer
can split an otherwise valid character. Initial tabs and line endings have
a separate positive response; a leading run of raw carriage returns is strongest.
