The component (layers.1.mlp.down_proj:3434) fires on the LaTeX display-math
delimiter "$$" (activation about 3.4 in either spacing form, "$$" or " $$"),
and very strongly on the "${" token that opens a math group (about 7; rare,
high-variance). Its activation does not depend on whether the delimiter opens
or closes the formula, so the program ignores context and looks up only the
current token. Smaller values go to block-level text delimiters that behave
alike: markdown code fences (```), double-backtick spans, and Python-style
triple quotes (docstring openers and closers). Every other token predicts 0;
the component's small diffuse noise is not modelled.
