"""Sparse approximation using slide/study vocabulary and document formatting.

The positive cues include slide headings, named study aids, instructional
'you should/will be able' phrases, and legacy bullet glyphs. Numbered slide
outlines strengthen HTML list markers. URL and opening metadata markers
have negative responses. Most tokens return zero: this does not explain
the component's many small lexical responses.

A bounded text tail and incomplete UTF-8 bytes handle split words/symbols;
all state resets when the document changes.
