"""Document beginnings and compact punctuation boundaries.

The first token has a large pulse, scaled by its broad character type.
Otherwise the component is nearly quiet. A period without a newline gets a
small response that grows with the run of letter-bearing tokens. Numbers
and short capitalized forms weaken it. Quoted list separators and function
arrows also respond. The run resets at document boundaries, newlines,
periods, semicolons, braces and East Asian sentence punctuation.
